

Phase 4 — Adaptive Multi-Agent Loop (Completed ✅)
Goal
Establish a clean, reliable, adaptive multi-agent execution loop with explicit boundaries between planning, execution, evaluation, and decision-making — enabling retries, learning, and future planners without refactors.

Architecture Overview

User Intent
   ↓
Planner
   ↓
Execution Plan (Steps)
   ↓
Parallel Executor
   ↓
Runtime Signals + Warnings
   ↓
Evaluator
   ↓
Loop Decision (ACCEPT / REPLAN / ABORT)
   ↺ (feedback via planner knobs)

Core Responsibilities
Planner
* Produces a Plan (ordered DAG of Steps)
* Reads:
    * ctx.intent
    * ctx.scratch["planner_knobs"]
* Outputs:
    * Steps with tools, args, resources, and timeouts
* Does not:
    * Execute steps
    * Emit verdicts
    * Inspect warnings directly

Executor (ParallelExecutor)
* Executes the DAG with:
    * dependency ordering
    * resource locks
    * per-step timeouts
* Emits runtime signals, not decisions:
    * step.runtime events
    * warnings (Step timeout, Step slow, etc.)
* Enforces SLAs but does not decide retries

Evaluator
* Observes outcomes:
    * results
    * warnings
    * runtime signals
* Computes:
    * planner_signals (facts)
    * planner_knobs (recommended changes for next attempt)
* Returns a recommendation:
    * ACCEPT
    * REPLAN
    * ABORT
* Does not emit events

Loop (Orchestrator)
* Owns control flow:
    * attempts
    * retries
    * final acceptance
* Handles:
    * timeout vs non-timeout failures
    * last-attempt best-effort logic
* Single authority for verdict emission
    * All verdicts go through _emit_verdict(...)
    * Ensures consistent payload (attempt_index, confidence, reason)

Feedback Loop (Key Phase-4 Achievement)
Signals → Knobs → Plan Changes
Example:
* Executor emits step.runtime → timeout detected
* Evaluator computes:    {
*   "timeout_overrides": {
*     "hotel.search": 50
*   }
* }
*   
* Planner reads knobs → increases timeout
* Next attempt runs with adapted plan
This loop converges or exits safely.

Reliability & Safety Guarantees
* Max attempts enforced
* Best-effort acceptance on final timeout
* Fatal errors short-circuit immediately
* JSON-safe scratch state (no sets, no non-serializable objects)
* Deterministic attempt indexing

Discipline Enforced
* ❌ No direct make_event("verdict", …) calls anywhere
* ✅ All verdicts emitted via _emit_verdict() in loop.py
* Executors signal, evaluators recommend, loop decides
This creates a hard Phase-4 boundary that future work builds on.

Phase 4 Status
✅ Complete
You now have:
* A true multi-agent feedback loop
* Clear planner ↔ executor ↔ evaluator contracts
* Stable runtime signaling
* A foundation for learning, arbitration, and APIs

7 Functional Agents:
Tier 1 – Cognitive
    • LLMPlannerAgent

Tier 2 – Domain
    • FlightAgent
    • HotelAgent
    • BundleAgent

Tier 3 – Intelligence
    • RankerAgent
    • EnrichAgent
    • GeoAgent

Folder Structure:

travel_agent/
  pyproject.toml                   # or requirements.txt
  main.py                          # python3 main.py "run query" ...
  README.md
  env.sh
  .gitignore

  travel_agent/
    __init__.py
    version.py

    cli/
      __init__.py
      main.py                      # python -m travel_agent ...
      run_query.py                 # python3 main.py "run query" ...
      commands/
        __init__.py
        run.py                     # run multi-agent loop
        replay.py                  # replay from stored run
        debug.py                   # print plan/graph/events/warnings
        bench.py                   # optional: quick perf checks

    contracts/                     # stable dataclasses/types (system API)
      __init__.py
      intent.py                    # UserIntent, Constraints, PassengerInfo...
      context.py                   # SharedContext (state + artifacts + budgets)
      plan.py                      # Plan, Step, ToolCall, StopConditions
      result.py                    # canonical results (Flight/Hotel/Bundle)
      warnings.py                  # Warning codes + structured warning payloads

      events.py                    # Event types (immutable): StepStarted, ToolCalled...
      messages.py                  # Message types for bus (commands + observations)
      protocols.py                 # Protocols/Interfaces: Agent, Tool, Bus, Store

    orchestrator/                  # adaptive loop + execution engine
      __init__.py

      loop.py                      # adaptive loop: plan -> execute -> evaluate -> replan
      policies.py                  # retry/relax/budget/stop rules
      evaluation.py                # verdict: ACCEPT/REPLAN/ABORT + confidence

      registry.py                  # agent registry + tool registry
      wiring.py                    # assemble system: agents/tools/bus/store (composition root)
      planner.py

      bus/                         # OPTIONAL UPGRADE: message bus
        __init__.py
        base.py                    # Bus interface (publish/subscribe)
        inproc.py                  # in-process pub/sub, routing rules
        router.py                  # topic routing / fanout / filters
        middleware.py              # logging/metrics/retry wrappers for bus
        topics.py                  # canonical topic names (strings/Enums)

      exec/                        # OPTIONAL UPGRADE: parallel execution engine
        __init__.py
        base.py                    # Executor interface
        sequential.py              # default: deterministic sequential executor
        parallel.py                # parallel executor (ThreadPoolExecutor)
        dag.py                     # build dependency graph from Plan steps
        scheduler.py               # schedule ready steps, handle joins/cancels
        locks.py                   # per-resource locks (provider/cache) if needed
        timeouts.py                # step timeouts + cancellation helpers

    agents/                        # actual agents (decision-making units)
      __init__.py
      base.py                      # Agent base, helpers, access patterns

      planner/                     # Planner family
        __init__.py
        rule_based.py              # deterministic planner (Phase 4 baseline)
        adaptive.py                # replan rules: relax constraints, alt airports/dates
        llm_based.py               # optional later behind flag (keep isolated)

      executors/                   # “doers”
        __init__.py
        flight_agent.py            # search flights tool calls -> ctx artifacts
        hotel_agent.py             # search hotels
        bundle_agent.py            # bundle endpoint OR compose flight+hotel
        compose_agent.py           # explicitly handles "soft-bundle" composition
        retry.py                   # retryConfig

      critics/                     # “judges”
        __init__.py
        validator_agent.py         # validate results + emit warnings/confidence
        ranker_agent.py            # scoring/ranking/dedupe
        cost_guard_agent.py        # enforces provider call budgets

      support/                     # helpers that still act as agents
        __init__.py
        geo_agent.py               # city/airport alternatives, radius broadening
        enrich_agent.py            # enrich-top-n bounded calls
        explainer_agent.py         # human-readable explanation from ctx+events

      listeners/                   # OPTIONAL UPGRADE: bus subscribers
        __init__.py
        trace_listener.py          # listens to events/messages, writes to ctx trace
        metrics_listener.py        # counters/timings
        store_listener.py          # persists run artifacts incrementally
        debug_listener.py          # prints live stream in --verbose

    tools/                         # pure I/O and utilities (NOT agents)
      __init__.py

      providers/
        __init__.py
        base.py                    # Provider interfaces
        amadeus/
          __init__.py
          client.py
          flights.py
          flight_agent_wrapper.py
          flight_availabilities.py
          hotels.py
          bundle.py

      cache/
        __init__.py
        base.py
        file.py
        memory.py
        key.py

      geo/
        __init__.py
        airports.csv
        resolver.py

      ranking/                     # pure functions used by ranker_agent
        __init__.py
        flight.py
        hotel.py
        bundle.py
        scoring.py

    runtime/                       # system plumbing (runs, serialization, logging)
      __init__.py
      run_id.py
      serialization.py             # ctx/plan/events/messages <-> json
      logging.py                   # structured logger config
      telemetry/
        __init__.py
        counters.py
        timings.py
      store/
        __init__.py
        base.py                    # Store interface
        file_store.py              # write runs/*.json
        sqlite_store.py            # optional indexing/querying
      replay/
        __init__.py
        player.py                  # replay a run by re-emitting events/messages

    nlp/                           # parsing + normalization into contracts.Intent
      __init__.py
      rule_parser.py
      enrich.py                    # if used for NLP-level enrichment
      normalize/
        __init__.py
        base.py
        flight.py
        hotel.py
        bundle.py

  tests/
    __init__.py
    test_smoke.py
    test_planner_rule_based.py
    test_orchestrator_loop.py
    test_bus_inproc.py             # optional upgrade tests
